        "title": "Thirty Years\nin the Making",
        "body_text": "<p>“I did the thing that women like me were not expected to do in that industry, in those years. I opened my own company.”</p><p>Laura Milman learned the diamond trade from the inside, working alongside her brother Jacob Arabo in the early years of what became Jacob &amp; Co. More than thirty years ago she opened her own company in New York's Diamond District, and she still sees clients in Midtown. Her house jewelry is designed in the city that trained her eye and brought to life by master goldsmiths in Italy.</p>",
        "signature": "— Laura Milman",
        "cta_text": "Read Laura's Story",
        "cta_url": "/pages/about",
        "portrait_image": "shopify://shop_images/laura-milman-portrait.jpg"
